1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:08,750
Chapter 31 My home then, when I at last find a home, is a cottage.

2
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:14,389
A little room with white washed walls and a sanded floor containing four painted

3
00:00:14,391 --> 00:00:19,410
chairs and a table, a clock, a cupboard, with two or three plates and dishes,

4
00:00:20,190 --> 00:00:21,870
and a set of tea-things in Delph.

5
00:00:22,849 --> 00:00:28,930
Above, a chamber of the same dimensions as the kitchen, with a deal bedstead and

6
00:00:28,930 --> 00:00:34,550
chest of drawers, small, yet too large to be filled with my scanty wardrobe.

7
00:00:35,449 --> 00:00:40,989
Though the kindness of my gentle and generous friends has increased that by a

8
00:00:40,991 --> 00:00:43,250
modest stock of such things as our necessary.

9
00:00:44,389 --> 00:00:45,529
It is evening.

10
00:00:46,430 --> 00:00:49,222
I have dismissed, with the fee of an orange,

11
00:00:49,222 --> 00:00:52,550
the little orphan who serves me as a handmaid.

12
00:00:53,029 --> 00:00:54,690
I am sitting alone on the hearth.

13
00:00:55,910 --> 00:00:58,930
This morning, the village school opened.

14
00:00:59,589 --> 00:01:05,430
I had twenty scholars, but three of the number can read, none right or cipher,

15
00:01:06,190 --> 00:01:08,550
several knit, and a few so a little.

16
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:12,269
They speak with the broadest accent of the district.

17
00:01:13,110 --> 00:01:17,730
At present, they and I have a difficulty in understanding each other's language.

18
00:01:18,849 --> 00:01:24,889
Some of them are unmanaged, rough, intractable, as well as ignorant,

19
00:01:25,449 --> 00:01:28,434
but others are docile, have a wish to learn,

20
00:01:28,434 --> 00:01:31,671
and events are disposition that pleases me.

21
00:01:32,209 --> 00:01:36,514
I must not forget that these coarsely clad little peasants are

22
00:01:36,514 --> 00:01:40,169
a flesh and blood as good as the science of gentlest genealogy.

23
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:47,809
And that the germs of native excellence, refinement, intelligence, kind feeling are

24
00:01:47,811 --> 00:01:51,150
as likely to exist in their hearts as in those of the best born.

25
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:55,529
My duty will be to develop these germs.

26
00:01:56,349 --> 00:02:00,489
Surely, I shall find some happiness in discharging that office.

27
00:02:01,370 --> 00:02:07,430
Much enjoyment I do not expect in the life opening before me, yet it will doubtless

28
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:10,811
if I regulate my mind and exert my powers as I

29
00:02:10,811 --> 00:02:14,750
ought, yield me enough to live on from day to day.

30
00:02:15,830 --> 00:02:22,190
Was I very gleeful, settled, content, during the hours I passed in Yonder Bayer

31
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:24,510
humble schoolroom this morning and afternoon?

32
00:02:25,510 --> 00:02:27,889
Not to deceive myself, I must reply.

33
00:02:28,669 --> 00:02:35,370
No, I felt desolate to a degree, I felt, yes, idiot that I am, I felt degraded.

34
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:38,805
I doubted I had taken a step which sank instead

35
00:02:38,807 --> 00:02:41,451
of raising me in the scale of social existence.

36
00:02:42,589 --> 00:02:49,110
I was weakly dismayed at the ignorance, the poverty, the coarseness of all I heard

37
00:02:49,110 --> 00:02:51,790
and saw around me, but let me not hate and

38
00:02:51,790 --> 00:02:55,150
despise myself too much for these feelings.

39
00:02:55,349 --> 00:02:57,910
I know them to be wrong, that is a great step gained.

40
00:02:58,690 --> 00:03:00,589
I shall strive to overcome them.

41
00:03:01,949 --> 00:03:05,690
Tomorrow I trust, I shall get the better of them partially.

42
00:03:06,529 --> 00:03:10,389
And in a few weeks perhaps, they will be quite subdued.

43
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:17,489
In a few months, it is possible, the happiness of seeing progress and a

44
00:03:17,491 --> 00:03:22,629
change for the better in my scholars may substitute gratification for disgust.

45
00:03:23,309 --> 00:03:27,349
Meantime, let me ask myself one question, which is better?

46
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:34,389
To have surrendered to temptation, listened to passion, made no painful

47
00:03:34,391 --> 00:03:41,449
effort, no struggle, but to have sunk down in the silken snare, fallen asleep on the

48
00:03:41,451 --> 00:03:47,690
flowers covering it, wakened in a southern climb amongst the luxuries of a pleasure

49
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:54,790
villa, to have been now living in France, Mr. Rochester's mistress, delirious,

50
00:03:55,029 --> 00:04:01,690
with his love half my time, for he would, oh yes, he would have loved me well for a

51
00:04:01,690 --> 00:04:06,089
while, he did love me, no one will ever love me so again.

52
00:04:07,230 --> 00:04:12,050
I shall never more know the sweet homage given to beauty, youth, and grace,

53
00:04:13,069 --> 00:04:16,089
for never do anyone else shall I seem to possess these charms.

54
00:04:17,150 --> 00:04:22,330
He was fond and proud of me, it is what no man besides will ever be.

55
00:04:22,989 --> 00:04:28,389
But where am I wondering, and what am I saying, and above all, feeling?

56
00:04:29,529 --> 00:04:35,050
Whether is it better, I ask, to be a slave in a fool's paradise at Marseille,

57
00:04:35,529 --> 00:04:40,470
fervored with delusive bliss one hour, suffocating with the bitterest tears of

58
00:04:40,470 --> 00:04:46,230
remorse and shame the next, or to be a village school mistress, free and honest,

59
00:04:46,970 --> 00:04:49,730
in a breezy mountain nook in the heart of England?

60
00:04:50,650 --> 00:04:58,370
Yes, I feel now that I was right when I adhered to principle and law, and scorned

61
00:04:58,370 --> 00:05:02,389
and crushed the insane promptings of a frenzied moment.

62
00:05:03,410 --> 00:05:08,449
God directed me to a correct choice, I thank his providence for the guidance.

63
00:05:09,709 --> 00:05:15,809
Having brought my even-tied musings to this point, I rose, went to my door,

64
00:05:16,669 --> 00:05:21,709
and looked at the sunset of the harvest day, and at the quiet fields before my

65
00:05:21,711 --> 00:05:26,510
cottage, which, with the school, was distant half a mile from the village.

66
00:05:27,510 --> 00:05:29,650
The birds were singing their last strains.

67
00:05:31,349 --> 00:05:35,050
The air was mild, the dew was barm.

68
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:42,769
While I looked, I thought myself happy, and was surprised to find myself air-long

69
00:05:42,771 --> 00:05:48,790
weeping, and why, for the doom which had left me from adhesion to my master,

70
00:05:49,669 --> 00:05:55,029
for him I was no more to see, for the desperate grief and fatal fury,

71
00:05:55,809 --> 00:06:01,190
consequences of my departure, which might now perhaps be dragging him from the path

72
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:05,370
of right, too far to leave hope of ultimate restoration, thither.

73
00:06:06,309 --> 00:06:09,997
At this thought, I turned my face aside from the

74
00:06:09,999 --> 00:06:13,569
lovely sky of Eve, and lonely veil of Morton.

75
00:06:14,269 --> 00:06:15,269
I say lonely.

76
00:06:15,949 --> 00:06:19,589
For in that bend of it visible to me, there was no building apparent,

77
00:06:20,069 --> 00:06:25,510
save the church and the passing-age, half-hidden trees, and, quite at the

78
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:32,031
extremity, the roof of veil hall, where the rich Mr. Oliver and his daughter lived.

79
00:06:32,370 --> 00:06:36,910
I hid my eyes, and lent my head against the stone frame of my door.

80
00:06:37,610 --> 00:06:41,050
But soon, a slight noise near the wicket which shut in my

81
00:06:41,050 --> 00:06:44,449
tiny garden from the meadow beyond, it made me look up.

82
00:06:45,610 --> 00:06:53,129
A dog, old Carlo, Mr. Rivers' pointer, as I saw in a moment, was pushing the gate

83
00:06:53,131 --> 00:06:57,690
with his nose, and singin' himself lent upon it with folded arms.

84
00:06:58,389 --> 00:07:04,089
His brown knit, his gaze, grave almost to displeasure, fixed on me.

85
00:07:04,930 --> 00:07:05,930
I asked him to come in.

86
00:07:07,169 --> 00:07:08,470
No, I cannot stay.

87
00:07:09,110 --> 00:07:11,809
I have only brought you a little parcel my sisters left for you.

88
00:07:12,269 --> 00:07:15,389
I think it contains a color box, pencils and paper.

89
00:07:16,849 --> 00:07:18,690
I approached to take it.

90
00:07:19,290 --> 00:07:20,669
A welcome gift it was.

91
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:26,029
He examined my face, I thought, with austerity, as I came near.

92
00:07:27,089 --> 00:07:30,690
The traces of tears were doubtless, very visible upon it.

93
00:07:31,629 --> 00:07:35,110
Have you found your first day's work harder than you expected?

94
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:37,050
He asked.

95
00:07:37,650 --> 00:07:43,190
Oh no, on the contrary, I think in time I shall get on with my scholars very well.

96
00:07:44,029 --> 00:07:48,309
But perhaps your accommodations, your cottage, your

97
00:07:48,311 --> 00:07:51,029
furniture, have disappointed your expectations.

98
00:07:51,870 --> 00:07:57,050
They are in truth scanty enough, but I interrupted.

99
00:07:57,949 --> 00:08:02,849
My cottage is clean and weatherproof, my furniture sufficient and commodious.

100
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:07,129
All I see has made me thankful, not despondent.

101
00:08:07,889 --> 00:08:11,747
I am not absolutely such a fool and sensualist, as to

102
00:08:11,749 --> 00:08:15,209
regret the absence of a carpet, a sofa and silver plate.

103
00:08:16,110 --> 00:08:19,169
Besides, five weeks ago, I had nothing.

104
00:08:19,830 --> 00:08:22,029
I was an outcast, a beggar, a vagrant.

105
00:08:22,769 --> 00:08:25,330
Now I have acquaintance, a home, a business.

106
00:08:25,330 --> 00:08:28,875
I wonder at the goodness of God, the generosity of

107
00:08:28,875 --> 00:08:32,669
my friends, the bounty of my lot, I do not repine.

108
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:36,370
But you feel solitude and oppression.

109
00:08:37,610 --> 00:08:40,849
The little house there behind you is dark and empty.

110
00:08:41,970 --> 00:08:45,817
I have hardly had time yet to enjoy a sense of tranquility,

111
00:08:45,819 --> 00:08:48,949
much less to grow impatient under one of loneliness.

112
00:08:50,650 --> 00:08:51,650
Very well.

113
00:08:52,410 --> 00:08:54,830
I hope you feel the content you express.

114
00:08:55,529 --> 00:08:59,641
At any rate, your good sense will tell you that it is too

115
00:08:59,642 --> 00:09:03,269
soon yet to yield to the vacillating fears of Lot's wife.

116
00:09:04,370 --> 00:09:08,430
What you had left before I saw you, of course I do not know.

117
00:09:09,209 --> 00:09:14,650
But I counsel you to resist firmly every temptation, which would incline you to

118
00:09:14,650 --> 00:09:20,029
look back, pursue your present career steadily, for some months at least.

119
00:09:21,709 --> 00:09:24,410
It is what I mean to do, I answered.

120
00:09:25,349 --> 00:09:31,089
Shingin continued, it is hard work to control the workings of inclination and

121
00:09:31,091 --> 00:09:36,050
turn the bent of nature, but that it may be done, I know from experience.

122
00:09:36,930 --> 00:09:41,589
God has given us, in a measure, the power to make our own fate,

123
00:09:42,470 --> 00:09:47,730
and when our energies seem to demand a sustenance they cannot get, when our will

124
00:09:47,730 --> 00:09:51,834
strains after a path we may not follow, we need neither

125
00:09:51,836 --> 00:09:56,169
starve from inclination nor stand still in despair.

126
00:09:57,029 --> 00:10:02,690
We have but to seek another nourishment for the mind, as strong as the forbidden

127
00:10:02,690 --> 00:10:09,370
food it long to taste, and perhaps pure, and to hue out for the adventurous foot,

128
00:10:09,849 --> 00:10:14,069
a road as direct and broad as the one fortune has blocked up against us,

129
00:10:14,569 --> 00:10:15,669
if rougher than it.

130
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:20,957
A year ago, I was myself intensely miserable, because I

131
00:10:20,959 --> 00:10:24,610
thought I had made a mistake in entering the ministry.

132
00:10:25,769 --> 00:10:28,870
Its uniform duties weird me to death.

133
00:10:29,690 --> 00:10:34,309
I burnt for the more active life of the world, for the more exciting toils of a

134
00:10:34,311 --> 00:10:39,349
literary career, for the destiny of an artist, author, orator, anything,

135
00:10:39,910 --> 00:10:41,470
rather than that of a priest.

136
00:10:42,029 --> 00:10:46,349
Yes, the heart of a politician, of a soldier, of a votary of glory,

137
00:10:47,010 --> 00:10:52,169
a lover of renown, a lustre after power, beat under my curate surplus.

138
00:10:52,910 --> 00:10:53,910
I considered.

139
00:10:54,290 --> 00:10:58,849
My life was so wretched, it must be changed, or I must die.

140
00:11:00,150 --> 00:11:04,610
After a season of darkness and struggling, light broke and relief fell.

141
00:11:05,389 --> 00:11:09,309
My cramped existence all at once spread out to a plane without bounds.

142
00:11:10,230 --> 00:11:12,730
My powers heard a call from heaven to rise.

143
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:18,230
Gather their full strength, spread their wings, and mount beyond ken.

144
00:11:19,830 --> 00:11:21,690
God had an errand for me.

145
00:11:22,809 --> 00:11:29,510
To bear which afar, to deliver it well, skill and strength, courage and eloquence.

146
00:11:30,209 --> 00:11:34,790
The best qualifications of soldier, statesmen, and orator were all needed,

147
00:11:35,550 --> 00:11:38,550
for these all center in the good missionary.

148
00:11:39,910 --> 00:11:42,430
A missionary I resolved to be.

149
00:11:43,750 --> 00:11:48,709
From that moment, my state of mind changed, the fetters dissolved and dropped

150
00:11:48,711 --> 00:11:52,082
from every faculty, leaving nothing of bondage

151
00:11:52,084 --> 00:11:55,769
but its galling sawness which time only can heal.

152
00:11:56,629 --> 00:12:00,110
My father, indeed, imposed the determination.

153
00:12:01,069 --> 00:12:05,849
But since his death, I have not a legitimate obstacle to contend with.

154
00:12:06,449 --> 00:12:13,089
Some affairs settled, a successor for Morton provided, an entanglement or two of

155
00:12:13,091 --> 00:12:15,550
the feelings broken through or cut us under.

156
00:12:16,330 --> 00:12:20,889
A last conflict with human weakness, in which I know I shall overcome,

157
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:24,290
because I have vowed that I will overcome.

158
00:12:24,989 --> 00:12:27,529
And I leave Europe for the East.

159
00:12:28,470 --> 00:12:35,410
He said this, in his peculiar subdued yet emphatic voice, looking when he had ceased

160
00:12:35,411 --> 00:12:40,489
speaking not at me, but at the setting sun at which I looked too.

161
00:12:42,430 --> 00:12:47,389
Both he and I had our backs towards the path leading up the field to the wicked.

162
00:12:48,069 --> 00:12:51,510
We had heard no step on that grass-grown track.

163
00:12:52,330 --> 00:12:56,949
The water running in the veil was the one lulling sound of the hour and scene.

164
00:12:58,010 --> 00:13:04,110
We might well then start, when a gay voice, sweet as a silver bell exclaimed.

165
00:13:05,230 --> 00:13:06,790
Good evening, Mr. Rivers.

166
00:13:07,910 --> 00:13:09,949
And good evening, old Carlo.

167
00:13:11,169 --> 00:13:14,610
Your dog is quicker to recognize his friends than you are, sir.

168
00:13:15,449 --> 00:13:19,269
He pricked his ears and wagged his tail when I was at the bottom of the field,

169
00:13:19,889 --> 00:13:21,629
and you have your back towards me now.

170
00:13:22,489 --> 00:13:23,610
It was true.

171
00:13:24,629 --> 00:13:30,029
Though Mr. Rivers had started at the first of those musical accents, as if a

172
00:13:30,031 --> 00:13:36,949
thunderbolt had split a cloud over his head, he stood yet at the close of the

173
00:13:36,951 --> 00:13:41,209
sentence, in the same attitude in which the speaker had surprised him,

174
00:13:41,750 --> 00:13:46,029
his arm resting on the gate, his face directed towards the west.

175
00:13:46,650 --> 00:13:49,930
He turned at last with measured deliberation.

176
00:13:50,849 --> 00:13:54,330
A vision, as it seemed to me, had risen at his side.

177
00:13:54,949 --> 00:14:00,870
There appeared, within three feet of him, a form clad in pure white, a youthful,

178
00:14:00,989 --> 00:14:07,069
graceful form, full, yet fine in contour, and when, after bending to caress Carlo,

179
00:14:07,489 --> 00:14:10,629
it lifted up its head, and threw back a long veil.

180
00:14:11,589 --> 00:14:15,069
They are bloomed under his glance a face of perfect beauty.

181
00:14:15,809 --> 00:14:21,910
Perfect beauty is a strong expression, but I do not retrace or qualify it.

182
00:14:22,430 --> 00:14:28,750
As sweet features as ever, the temperate climb of Albion moulded, as pure hues of

183
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:34,230
rows and lily, as ever her humid gales and vapoury skies generated and screened,

184
00:14:34,629 --> 00:14:37,349
justified in this instance, the term.

185
00:14:38,209 --> 00:14:42,269
No charm was wanting, no defect was perceptible.

186
00:14:43,129 --> 00:14:48,529
The young girl had regular and delicate lineaments, eyes shaped and coloured,

187
00:14:48,531 --> 00:14:53,010
as we see them in lovely pictures large and dark and full.

188
00:14:54,169 --> 00:15:00,110
The long and shadowy eyelash which encircles a fine eye with so soft a fascination.

189
00:15:00,610 --> 00:15:05,410
The penciled brow which gives such clearness, the white smooth forehead,

190
00:15:05,910 --> 00:15:11,430
which adds such repose to the livelier beauties of tint and ray, the cheek oval,

191
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:18,269
fresh and smooth, the lips, fresh too, ruddy, healthy, sweetly formed,

192
00:15:18,529 --> 00:15:24,029
the even and gleaming teeth without flaw, the small dimpled chin, the ornament of

193
00:15:24,031 --> 00:15:28,557
rich, plentiest tresses, all advantages in short, which

194
00:15:28,557 --> 00:15:32,889
combined, realised the ideal of beauty, were fully hers.

195
00:15:33,769 --> 00:15:39,410
I wondered, as I looked at this fair creature, I admired her with my whole

196
00:15:39,411 --> 00:15:46,029
heart, nature had surely formed her in a partial mood, and forgetting her usual

197
00:15:46,031 --> 00:15:49,540
stinted stepmother doll of gifts, had endowed

198
00:15:49,542 --> 00:15:52,911
this her darling, with a grand am's bounty.

199
00:15:54,209 --> 00:15:58,650
What did Singen Rivers think of this earthly angel?

200
00:15:59,589 --> 00:16:04,489
I naturally asked myself that question, as I saw him turn to her and look at her,

201
00:16:05,069 --> 00:16:09,529
and as naturally I sought the answer to the inquiry in his countenance.

202
00:16:10,410 --> 00:16:13,902
He had already withdrawn his eye from the Perry, and was

203
00:16:13,904 --> 00:16:17,410
looking at a humble tuft of daisies which grew by the wicked.

204
00:16:19,110 --> 00:16:25,709
A lovely evening, but late for you to be out alone, he said, as he crushed the

205
00:16:25,711 --> 00:16:28,930
snowy heads of the closed flowers with his foot.

206
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:32,591
Oh, I only came home from... she mentioned the

207
00:16:32,593 --> 00:16:36,031
name of a large town some 20 miles distant.

208
00:16:36,610 --> 00:16:37,610
This afternoon.

209
00:16:38,650 --> 00:16:43,050
Pappar told me you had opened your school, and that the new mistress was come,

210
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:48,430
and so I put on my bonnet after tea, and ran up the valley to see her.

211
00:16:48,989 --> 00:16:50,690
This is she, pointing to me.

212
00:16:51,470 --> 00:16:52,930
It is said Singen.

213
00:16:54,529 --> 00:16:56,230
Do you think you shall like Morton?

214
00:16:56,769 --> 00:17:00,910
She asked of me, with a direct and naive simplicity of tone and manner,

215
00:17:01,529 --> 00:17:02,750
pleasing if childlike.

216
00:17:03,750 --> 00:17:04,750
I hope I shall.

217
00:17:05,330 --> 00:17:06,910
I have many inducements to do so.

218
00:17:08,629 --> 00:17:12,069
Did you find your scholars as attentive as you expected?

219
00:17:12,870 --> 00:17:13,870
Quite.

220
00:17:14,010 --> 00:17:15,089
Do you like your house?

221
00:17:15,489 --> 00:17:16,489
Very much.

222
00:17:16,629 --> 00:17:17,709
Have I furnished it nicely?

223
00:17:18,569 --> 00:17:19,910
Very nicely indeed.

224
00:17:20,970 --> 00:17:23,750
And made a good choice of an attendant for you in Alice Wood.

225
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:26,050
You have indeed.

226
00:17:26,830 --> 00:17:28,209
She is teachable and handy.

227
00:17:29,389 --> 00:17:35,392
This, then, I thought, is Miss Oliver the Ares, favored, it

228
00:17:35,394 --> 00:17:39,750
seems, in the gifts of fortune, as well as in those of nature.

229
00:17:40,650 --> 00:17:45,690
What happy combination of the planets presided over her birth, I wonder.

230
00:17:46,910 --> 00:17:51,430
I shall come up and help you to teach sometimes, she added.

231
00:17:52,470 --> 00:17:55,209
It will be a change for me to visit you now and then.

232
00:17:55,970 --> 00:17:57,769
And I like a change.

233
00:17:58,389 --> 00:18:02,669
Mr. Rivers, I have been so gay during my stay at S.

234
00:18:03,389 --> 00:18:08,150
Last night, or rather this morning, I was dancing till two o'clock.

235
00:18:09,510 --> 00:18:13,167
The Wath Regiment a station there since the riots, and

236
00:18:13,167 --> 00:18:16,650
the officers are the most agreeable men in the world.

237
00:18:17,169 --> 00:18:20,709
They put all our young knife grinders and sysa merchants to shame.

238
00:18:22,529 --> 00:18:26,091
It seemed to me that Mr. Syngen's underlip

239
00:18:26,091 --> 00:18:30,491
protruded, and his upper lip curled a moment.

240
00:18:30,930 --> 00:18:36,110
His mouth certainly looked a good deal compressed, and the lower part of his face

241
00:18:36,110 --> 00:18:41,849
unusually stern and square, as the laughing girl gave him this information.

242
00:18:42,910 --> 00:18:46,930
He lifted his gaze to from the daisies, and turned it on her.

243
00:18:47,690 --> 00:18:50,589
An unsmiling, a searching, a meaning gaze it was.

244
00:18:51,629 --> 00:18:56,410
She answered it, with a second laugh, and laughter well became her youth,

245
00:18:56,889 --> 00:18:59,169
her roses, her dimples, her bright eyes.

246
00:19:00,169 --> 00:19:06,150
As he stood, mute and grave, she again fell to caressing Carlo.

247
00:19:07,089 --> 00:19:09,430
Poor Carlo loves me, said she.

248
00:19:10,089 --> 00:19:13,970
He is not stern and distant to his friends, and if he could speak,

249
00:19:14,550 --> 00:19:15,550
he would not be silent.

250
00:19:16,169 --> 00:19:21,750
As she patted the dog's head, bending with native grace before his young and austere

251
00:19:21,750 --> 00:19:25,830
master, I saw a glow rise to that master's face.

252
00:19:26,809 --> 00:19:33,271
I saw his solemn eye melt with sudden fire, and flicker with resisteless emotion.

253
00:19:34,089 --> 00:19:38,470
Flushed and kindled thus, he looked nearly as beautiful for a man as she,

254
00:19:38,750 --> 00:19:39,750
for a woman.

255
00:19:40,169 --> 00:19:47,089
His chest heaved once, as if his large heart, weary of despotic constriction,

256
00:19:47,510 --> 00:19:50,834
had expanded, despite the will, and made a

257
00:19:50,836 --> 00:19:53,449
vigorous bound for the attainment of liberty.

258
00:19:54,370 --> 00:19:59,970
But he curbed it, I think, as a resolute rider would curb a rearing steed.

259
00:20:00,669 --> 00:20:06,110
He responded neither by word nor movement to the gentle advances made him.

260
00:20:07,529 --> 00:20:12,349
Papa says you never come to see us now, continued Miss Oliver, looking up.

261
00:20:13,129 --> 00:20:15,690
You are quite a stranger at Vale Hall.

262
00:20:16,550 --> 00:20:19,389
He has alone this evening, and not very well.

263
00:20:20,550 --> 00:20:22,389
Will you return with me and visit him?

264
00:20:24,230 --> 00:20:28,410
It is not a seasonable hour to intrude on Mr. Oliver, answered Syngen.

265
00:20:29,050 --> 00:20:32,449
Not a seasonable hour, but I declare it is.

266
00:20:33,089 --> 00:20:36,330
It is just the hour when Papa most wants company.

267
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:41,273
When the works are closed and he has no business to occupy him, now Mr.

268
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:43,550
Rivers, do come.

269
00:20:43,650 --> 00:20:46,330
Why are you so very shy and so very somber?

270
00:20:47,589 --> 00:20:49,150
She filled up the hiatus.

271
00:20:49,970 --> 00:20:52,430
His silence left by a reply of her own.

272
00:20:53,290 --> 00:21:01,050
I forgot, she exclaimed, shaking her beautiful curled head as if shocked at herself.

273
00:21:01,550 --> 00:21:03,510
I am so giddy and thoughtless.

274
00:21:04,309 --> 00:21:05,309
Do excuse me.

275
00:21:06,029 --> 00:21:08,078
It had slipped my memory that you have good

276
00:21:08,078 --> 00:21:10,991
reasons to be indisposed for joining in my chatter.

277
00:21:11,790 --> 00:21:17,190
Diana and Mary have left you, and more house is shut up, and you are so lonely.

278
00:21:17,989 --> 00:21:19,389
I am sure I pity you.

279
00:21:19,830 --> 00:21:20,830
Do come and see Papa.

280
00:21:22,430 --> 00:21:24,110
Not tonight, Ms. Rosamond.

281
00:21:24,769 --> 00:21:25,769
Not tonight.

282
00:21:26,489 --> 00:21:28,930
Mr. Syngen spoke almost like an automaton.

283
00:21:29,889 --> 00:21:32,750
Himself only knew the effort it cost him thus to refuse.

284
00:21:33,889 --> 00:21:37,529
Well, if you are so obstinate, I will leave you.

285
00:21:38,150 --> 00:21:39,690
For I dare not stay any longer.

286
00:21:40,250 --> 00:21:41,370
The dew begins to fall.

287
00:21:42,069 --> 00:21:43,069
Good evening.

288
00:21:43,690 --> 00:21:45,089
She held out her hand.

289
00:21:45,870 --> 00:21:46,870
He just touched it.

290
00:21:47,650 --> 00:21:49,309
Good evening, he repeated.

291
00:21:49,870 --> 00:21:51,569
In a voice low and hollow as an echo.

292
00:21:52,169 --> 00:21:53,169
She turned.

293
00:21:53,330 --> 00:21:54,910
But in a moment returned.

294
00:21:56,230 --> 00:21:57,230
Are you well?

295
00:21:57,489 --> 00:21:58,489
She asked.

296
00:21:58,730 --> 00:22:00,010
Well might she put the question.

297
00:22:00,510 --> 00:22:02,110
His face was blanched as her gown.

298
00:22:02,709 --> 00:22:04,930
Quite well, he enunciated.

299
00:22:05,309 --> 00:22:07,150
And with a bow, he left the gate.

300
00:22:08,629 --> 00:22:09,690
She went one way.

301
00:22:10,190 --> 00:22:11,190
He another.

302
00:22:11,269 --> 00:22:15,050
She turned twice to gaze after him as she tripped fairy light down the field.

303
00:22:15,790 --> 00:22:19,970
He, as he strode firmly across, never turned at all.

304
00:22:21,809 --> 00:22:24,631
This spectacle of another's suffering and sacrifice

305
00:22:24,631 --> 00:22:28,870
wrapped my thoughts from exclusive meditation on my own.

306
00:22:30,370 --> 00:22:36,129
Diana Rivers had designated her brother, inexorable as death.

307
00:22:36,970 --> 00:22:38,690
She had not exaggerated.
